Input: {"question": "When was the Pugh House built?", "source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0302-fc2a7347bbb5:d00", "start": 0, "end": 223, "text": "Captain David Pugh House The Captain David Pugh House is a historic 19th-century Federal-style residence on the Cacapon River in the unincorporated community of Hooks Mills in Hampshire County, West Virginia, United States."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0302-fc2a7347bbb5:d00", "start": 224, "end": 278, "text": "It is also known by its current farm name, Riversdell."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0302-fc2a7347bbb5:d00", "start": 279, "end": 323, "text": "It is a -story frame dwelling built in 1835."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0302-fc2a7347bbb5:d00", "start": 324, "end": 394, "text": "It sits on a stone foundation and has a -story addition built in 1910."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0302-fc2a7347bbb5:d00", "start": 395, "end": 491, "text": "The front facade features a centered porch with shed roof supported by two Tuscan order columns."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0302-fc2a7347bbb5:d00", "start": 492, "end": 565, "text": "The rear has a two-story, full-width porch recessed under the gable roof."}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0302-fc2a7347bbb5:d00", "start": 566, "end": 592, "text": "Also on the property are a"}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0302-fc2a7347bbb5:d01", "start": 0, "end": 123, "text": "Pugh House (Morrisville, North Carolina) Pugh House is a historic home located at Morrisville, Wake County, North Carolina."}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0302-fc2a7347bbb5:d01", "start": 124, "end": 260, "text": "The house was built about 1870, and is a two-story, three-bay-wide, Italianate style frame I-house with a one-story end-gabled rear ell."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0302-fc2a7347bbb5:d01", "start": 261, "end": 390, "text": "It features molded roof cornice brackets with finials, bargeboards with fleur-de-lis-shaped motifs, and a hip roofed front porch."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0302-fc2a7347bbb5:d01", "start": 391, "end": 444, "text": "Also on the property is a contributing smokehouse (c."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0302-fc2a7347bbb5:d01", "start": 445, "end": 451, "text": "1880)."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0302-fc2a7347bbb5:d01", "start": 452, "end": 550, "text": "The house and smokehouse were moved from 10018 Chapel Hill Road to their present location in 2008."}, "D2S7": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0302-fc2a7347bbb5:d01", "start": 551, "end": 628, "text": "It was the home of artist Mabel Pugh (1891–1986), who sold the house in 1958."}, "D2S8": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0302-fc2a7347bbb5:d01", "start": 629, "end": 631, "text": "It"}, "D3S1": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0302-fc2a7347bbb5:d02", "start": 0, "end": 28, "text": "in the Pugh family cemetery."}, "D3S2": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0302-fc2a7347bbb5:d02", "start": 29, "end": 163, "text": "Jesse Pickens Pugh Farmstead The Jesse Pickens Pugh Farmstead is a historic homestead near Grove Hill in rural Clarke County, Alabama."}, "D3S3": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0302-fc2a7347bbb5:d02", "start": 164, "end": 272, "text": "The homestead contains seven contributing buildings, two contributing sites, and one contributing structure."}, "D3S4": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0302-fc2a7347bbb5:d02", "start": 273, "end": 400, "text": "These include a half-spraddle roof cottage that was built in 1865, agricultural outbuildings, agricultural fields, and burials."}, "D3S5": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0302-fc2a7347bbb5:d02", "start": 401, "end": 524, "text": "The complex was listed on the National Register of Historic Places on July 28, 1999, due to its architectural significance."}, "D3S6": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0302-fc2a7347bbb5:d02", "start": 525, "end": 597, "text": "Jesse Pickens Pugh was born on April 17, 1829 in Clarke County, Alabama."}, "D3S7": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0302-fc2a7347bbb5:d02", "start": 598, "end": 643, "text": "He was the son of Isaac Pugh, born in 1785 in"}, "D4S1": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0302-fc2a7347bbb5:d03", "start": 0, "end": 125, "text": "do in Ottawa , Montreal , or her favourite spot—Disney World—Helena hopes to leave readers dreaming of their next adventure ."}, "D4S2": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0302-fc2a7347bbb5:d03", "start": 126, "end": 552, "text": "Related Here 's where Paul Bernardo is now and what 's happened since he went to prison in 1995 Helena Hanson November 26 , 2024 A BC man who escaped prison is on Canada 's Most Wanted list and may be 'armed and dangerous ' Morgan Leet December 05 , 2024 Infamous Canadian killer Paul Bernardo is set to appear before Canada 's parole board today Narcity Trending Staff November 26 , 2024 Advertisement © All rights reserved ,"}, "D5S1": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0302-fc2a7347bbb5:d04", "start": 0, "end": 459, "text": ") Bosnia Herzegovina Convertible Mark ( BAM ) Botswana Pula ( BWP ) Brazilian Real ( BRL ) Bulgarian Lev ( BGN ) Canadian Dollar ( CAD ) Cayman Islands Dollar ( KYD ) Cfp Franc ( XPF ) Chilean Peso ( CLP ) Chinese Yuan ( CNY ) Colombian Peso ( COP ) Costa Rican Colón ( CRC ) Croatian Kuna ( HRK ) Czech Koruna ( CZK ) Danish Krone ( DKK ) Dominican Peso ( DOP ) East Caribbean Dollar ( XCD ) Egyptian Pound ( EGP ) Fijian Dollar ( FJD ) Great British Pound ("}}, "candidates": [{"candidate_id": "C0", "answer": "1835", "card_ids": ["ramdocs-0302-fc2a7347bbb5:d00:c0"]}, {"candidate_id": "C1", "answer": "about 1870", "card_ids": ["ramdocs-0302-fc2a7347bbb5:d01:c0"]}, {"candidate_id": "C2", "answer": "1865", "card_ids": ["ramdocs-0302-fc2a7347bbb5:d02:c0"]}], "original_cards": [{"doc_id": "ramdocs-0302-fc2a7347bbb5:d00", "card_id": "ramdocs-0302-fc2a7347bbb5:d00:c0", "entity": "Captain David Pugh House", "scope": "Construction date", "claim": "The Captain David Pugh House was built in 1835.", "answer": "1835", "quote": "It is a -story frame dwelling built in 1835.", "original_document_number": 1}, {"doc_id": "ramdocs-0302-fc2a7347bbb5:d01", "card_id": "ramdocs-0302-fc2a7347bbb5:d01:c0", "entity": "Pugh House", "scope": "construction date", "claim": "The Pugh House was built about 1870.", "answer": "about 1870", "quote": "The house was built about 1870, and is a two-story, three-bay-wide, Italianate style frame I-house with a one-story end-gabled rear ell.", "original_document_number": 2}, {"doc_id": "ramdocs-0302-fc2a7347bbb5:d02", "card_id": "ramdocs-0302-fc2a7347bbb5:d02:c0", "entity": "half-spraddle roof cottage", "scope": "Jesse Pickens Pugh Farmstead", "claim": "A half-spraddle roof cottage at the Jesse Pickens Pugh Farmstead was built in 1865.", "answer": "1865", "quote": "These include a half-spraddle roof cottage that was built in 1865, agricultural outbuildings, agricultural fields, and burials.", "original_document_number": 3}], "initial_answers": ["1835", "about 1870"]}
